 "overview": {
  "summary": "Half of the calibrator's resistance function, and the half that does the thinking. A9 carries only three resistance values of its own -- 1 ohm, 1.9 ohm and a short -- but it holds all of the ohms calibration circuitry except one op amp, the two-wire lead drop compensation circuit, and the 82C55 Programmable Peripheral Interface (U11) whose three ports drive the relay latch/drivers on this board *and* on the Ohms Main assembly (A10). Four blocks make it up. The 2/5/10 V source (K9, Z1, U1, Q1, with Q2 and Q3 switching divider taps) is the current source behind every resistance ratio measurement the instrument makes. The differential amplifier (U2 and U3 in, U4 out, U5 cancelling the current through R18, gain 75 set by resistors in Z1) reads the result and sends it to A11's adc on the RCL line. The two-wire compensation circuit -- a 30 kHz dc-to-dc converter of U6 and T1 making a floating +/-8.2 V supply, chopper amplifier U7 with buffer U8 cancelling the high-side lead drop, and U10 sensing that current to make U9 cancel the low-side drop -- lets a two-wire ohmmeter be calibrated without its own lead resistance spoiling the result. And the digital section (U11, decoders U12 and U13, inverter U22, seven UCN5801 latch/drivers U14-U20 and diagnostic multiplexer U21) switches the board's 31 latching relays and reports the diagnostic lines back on SDL. The 1 ohm value is four 4 ohm wirewounds in parallel in R41; the 1.9 ohm value is two 3.8 ohm wirewounds in parallel in R42; K7 and K8 select the short.",
  "connectors": "P311 and P312, DIN 41612 type C, 64-pin right-angle. P311 carries the analog side -- OHMS OUT HI/LO, OHMS SENSE HI/LO, INT SENSE LO, OUT LO, DAC OUT HI/LO, DAC SENSE HI, 10V OUT HI, AMP IN, AMP OUT, ACOM, R COM, SDL and RCL. P312 carries the supplies (+/-17 S and S COM, +5 RLH and RLH COM, +5 LH, LH COM and -5 LH) and the guarded digital bus, and re-exports the 82C55's port lines to A10 as OHM PA0-PA7, OHM PB0-PB3 and OHM PC0-PC5.",
  "sections": "§2-173 … §2-185",
  "note": "A9 makes no supply of its own except the floating +/-8A pair for the compensation amplifiers. Everything else arrives on P312 from A17 and A19: +/-17 S with S COM for the analog circuits, +5 RLH with RLH COM for the relay drivers, and +5 LH / -5 LH with LH COM for the logic. Those are three different commons and only S COM has a test point (TP12); a meter left on TP12 reads the relay-driver and logic rails wrong. §4-14 also applies here in its strong form: A9 mounts component side to the REAR, so it needs the analog reverse extender card, and §5-10 step 1 has you take the rear shield off before probing."
 },
