   "title": "Step references are picked out of prose one token at a time",
   "text": "The designators highlighted on a procedure step are extracted token by token, so a range or a shared prefix in the printed sentence links only what is written out in full. On this board that is visible in step 2, where 'check relays K4, K5, K6, and the four wire-wound resistors in R41' links all four correctly, but any step that wrote a range would link only its endpoints. Read the sentence, not just the chips it lit up.",
