   "title": "MP4 is described as A14's shield",
   "text": "Table 6-10 gives MP4 as 'SHIELD, HIGH VOLTAGE CONTROL', Fluke 761197, in both revisions -- and High Voltage Control is A14, not A9. M4 on the same table is 'SHIELD, OHMS CAL', Fluke 775312. §5-10 step 1 refers to 'the rear shield' of this assembly in the singular. So A9's bill of materials carries two shields, one of which is named after another board. Nothing here resolves which physical part is which; both are recorded as printed, and the description of MP4 should not be taken as evidence about where the part goes.",
