   "title": "Three parts changed between the two revisions",
   "text": "Joining the two parts lists on Fluke stock number leaves exactly three rows that do not join, and all three are genuine revision differences rather than scanning errors. R11 is 'RESISTOR A52R,RES,MOX,330,+-5%,1W,200PPM' stock 689604 in the 1996 list and 'RES,CC,330,+-5%,1W' stock 163394, an Allen-Bradley GB3311, in Rev 9 -- a change from metal oxide to carbon composition, or rather back from it, since Rev 9 is the earlier revision and the one the photographed board matches. R25 is the same story at 150 ohm: 689612 metal oxide against 178566 carbon composition (GB1515). And VR1/VR2 are stock 386771 in 1996, described as 'ZENER 1N756A A52R', against 810309 in Rev 9 with manufacturer part 1N756ARR1 -- the same 8.2 V device under a different Fluke number. Each carries its Rev 9 row as asBuilt. Order against the 1996 numbers.",
